    "created_at": "2019-05-16T21:40:01Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-05-16T21:40:01Z",
    "body": "I should give more context here.\r\nUsing a weak set and liming its size looks like an unclear behavior to me, because each browser could have its own size limit and cause inconsistent behavior.\r\n\r\nThe basic idea of this proposal is that a rejected promise should be in one of following states,\r\n1). unhandled, `unhandledrejection` is not yet fired.\r\n2). unhandled, `unhandledrejection` is fired.\r\n3). handled\r\n\r\nThe `pending rejected promises set` contains only the promise that is in state 1). And the promise will eventually go into state 2) or 3), then be removed from set, so `pending rejected promises set` doesn't need to be a leak set nor limiting its size.\r\n\r\nThis is also how Gecko currently implements promise rejection event. ",
